Designing and Developing a data model
1. Create a relationship between Countries data and Exchange date
(1:1 cardinality, Cross filter both, Active relationship)
2. Create a relationship between the Sales and Countries tables
(Many:1 Cardinality, Cross filter both, Active relationship)
3. Create a relationship between the Purchases and Sales tables
(1:1 Cardinality, Cross filter both, Active relationship)
4. Dax - Configure the Calendar table by using NEw Table and a dax formula

        CalendarTable = 
        ADDCOLUMNS(
        CALENDAR(DATE(2020, 1, 1), DATE(2023, 12, 31)),
        "Year", YEAR([Date]),
        "Month Number", MONTH([Date]),
        "Month", FORMAT([Date], "MMMM"),
        "Quarter", QUARTER([Date]),
        "Weekday", WEEKDAY([Date]),
        "Day", DAY([Date])
        )

5. Create a relationship between the Calendar and Purchases tables
(Many:1 Cardinality, Active relationship)
6. Dax - Create a Sales in USD calculated table, using New Table

        Sales in USD = 
        ADDCOLUMNS(
            Sales,
            "Country Name", RELATED(Countries[Country]),
            "Exchange Rate", RELATED('Exchange Data'[Exchange Rate]),
            "Exchange Currency", RELATED('Exchange Data'[Exchange Currency]),
            "Gross Revenue USD", [Gross Revenue] * RELATED('Exchange Data'[Exchange Rate]),
            "Net Revenue USD", [Net Revenue] * RELATED('Exchange Data'[Exchange Rate]),
            "Total Tax USD", [Total Tax] * RELATED('Exchange Data'[Exchange Rate])
        )
7. Create a relationship between the Sales and Sales in USD
(1:1 Cardinality, Active relationship)

CREATING MEASURES FOR DATA STORYTELLING
1) Creating a measure to represent Yearly profit margin. Profit / Net Revenue. First I created a calculated column for Profit and used for the new measure.
2) Creating a measure to represent Quarterly profit. to use profit in USD, I CALCULATE THE COLUMN FIRST
3) Calculating Year-to-date Profit measure. USIN PROFIT IN USD
4) Calculating Year-to-date median sales measure from the sales table.


